"""
The public `std::time` facade.

This facade exposes typed monotonic timing, duration arithmetic, deadlines,
busy-wait delays, and provider-backed sleep. It deliberately does not expose
wall-clock, calendar, timezone, platform clock structures, raw pointers, or
the private runtime bridge symbols. Hosted availability is selected by the
standard-library runtime profile; unsupported profiles fail before emission.
"""
"""Keep implementation constants private to the time module."""
open config;

"""Re-export the typed time error variants used by fallible operations."""
open errors;

"""Re-export exact integer duration construction and arithmetic."""
open duration;

"""Re-export monotonic expiration and remaining-time operations."""
open deadline;

"""Re-export the short, scheduler-independent busy-wait delay."""
open delay;

"""Re-export monotonic instant capture and elapsed-time operations."""
open instant;

"""Re-export the private-provider-backed monotonic clock wrapper."""
open monotonic;

"""Re-export provider-backed scheduler-aware sleeping."""
open sleep;

"""Re-export allocation-free one-shot and periodic timer state machines."""
open timer;
